### ─── UPDATE & DELETE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §37. Update a single laptop — mark Dell XPS 15 back in stock and drop price
POST http://localhost:1538/update
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": {
    "lp2": { "in_stock": true, "price": 3456 }
  }
}

### §38. Update multiple laptops in one call
POST http://localhost:1538/update
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": {
    "lp1": { "price": 1399 },
    "lp6": { "price": 799 }
  }
}

### §39. Delete a single laptop by key
POST http://localhost:1538/delete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "keys": "lp6"
}

### §40. Delete multiple laptops in one call
POST http://localhost:1538/delete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "keys": ["lp4", "lp5"]
}

### §41. Drop an entire collection
POST http://localhost:1538/delete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "drop": true
}

### ─── RESTFUL GET ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §42. GET single laptop via REST endpoint
GET http://localhost:1538/collections/laptops/docs/lp2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### §43. GET all laptops via REST (paginated — first 3)
GET http://localhost:1538/collections/laptops?limit=3&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### §44. GET all laptops via REST (paginated — next 3)
GET http://localhost:1538/collections/laptops?limit=3&offset=3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ─── VERSIONING ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §45. Read lp2 — note the _v, createdAt, modifiedAt fields added by the engine
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "keys": "lp2"
}

### §46. Conflict test — send _v:1 when server already has _v:2 → write is skipped
### Run §39 first (which bumps lp4 to _v:2), then run this — it should be ignored.
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": {
    "lp4": { "brand": "Dell", "model": "XPS 15 STALE", "price": 999, "_v": 1 }
  }
}

### ─── EXTENDS (inline reference embedding at insert time) ────────────────────
### The "extend" key embeds data from another collection directly into the
### stored document at insert time. The referenced document is fetched once
### and stored as a snapshot — no join needed on reads.
### Format: "extend": { "<alias>": "<collection>.<key>", ... }
### The "extend" key is removed from the final stored document.

### §50. Insert lp7 with embedded memory and display via extend
### ram  → fetches mem4 from the memory collection and embeds it
### screen → fetches dsp3 from the display collection and embeds it
### After this insert, lp7 contains the full mem4 and dsp3 documents inline.
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": {
    "lp7": {
      "brand": "MSI",
      "model": "Titan GT77",
      "price": 3299,
      "in_stock": true,
      "tags": ["gaming", "desktop-replacement", "windows"],
      "specs": {
        "cpu": { "brand": "Intel", "cores": 16, "ghz": 5.0 },
        "battery_wh": 99,
        "weight_kg": 3.3
      },
      "extends": {
        "ram":    "memory.mem4",
        "screen": "display.dsp3"
      }
    }
  }
}

### §51. Read lp7 back — ram and screen are now full embedded documents, not pointers
### Expected: ram = { capacity_gb: 64, type: "DDR5", ... }, screen = { size_inch: 15.6, ... }
### The "extend" key is gone — it was consumed at insert time.
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "keys": "lp7"
}

### §52. extends with auto-generated key (array format)
### The extend block works identically when data is an array (UUIDv7 keys auto-assigned).
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": [
    {
      "brand": "HP",
      "model": "Spectre x360",
      "price": 1599,
      "in_stock": true,
      "extends": {
        "ram": "memory.mem2"
      }
    }
  ]
}

### §53. extends with a missing reference — insert still succeeds, alias simply not added
### "memory.mem99" does not exist — the insert completes without error,
### and the stored document will have brand/model/price but no "ram" field.
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": {
    "lp8": {
      "brand": "Lenovo",
      "model": "Legion 5",
      "price": 1199,
      "extend": {
        "ram": "memory.mem99"
      }
    }
  }
}

### ─── BULK DELETE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Delete all documents matching a `where` filter in a single request.
### Response: { "status": "ok", "deleted": <count> }
### The `count` param (optional) limits how many matching documents are deleted.

### §60. Bulk delete — remove all out-of-stock laptops
POST http://localhost:1538/delete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "where": {
    "in_stock": { "$eq": false }
  }
}

### §61. Bulk delete with a numeric filter — remove all laptops under £500
POST http://localhost:1538/delete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "where": {
    "price": { "$lt": 500 }
  }
}

### §62. Bulk delete with $or — remove all AMD or Apple laptops
POST http://localhost:1538/delete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "where": {
    "$or": [
      { "specs.cpu.brand": { "$eq": "AMD" } },
      { "specs.cpu.brand": { "$eq": "Apple" } }
    ]
  }
}

### §63. Bulk delete with count — remove at most 2 gaming laptops
### Useful for batched cleanup jobs that process large collections in chunks.
POST http://localhost:1538/delete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "where": {
    "tags": { "$contains": "gaming" }
  },
  "count": 2
}

### §64. Bulk delete — drop all documents in a collection via where: {}
### An empty where clause matches every document — equivalent to clearing the collection
### without dropping it (the collection itself remains, just empty).
POST http://localhost:1538/delete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "memory",
  "where": {}
}

### §65. maxSize -- register a capped collection (max 5 documents) via /schema
POST http://localhost:1538/schema
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "recent_events",
  "maxSize": 5
}

### §66. maxSize -- insert 3 documents into the capped collection
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "recent_events",
  "data": {
    "evt_001": { "type": "login",  "user": "alice" },
    "evt_002": { "type": "view",   "user": "bob" },
    "evt_003": { "type": "logout", "user": "alice" }
  }
}

### §67. maxSize -- insert 4 more documents (oldest 2 will be evicted, keeping only 5)
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "recent_events",
  "data": {
    "evt_004": { "type": "login",  "user": "carol" },
    "evt_005": { "type": "view",   "user": "carol" },
    "evt_006": { "type": "purchase", "user": "carol" },
    "evt_007": { "type": "logout", "user": "carol" }
  }
}

### §68. maxSize -- inline on /set (register cap and insert in one request)
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "top5_scores",
  "maxSize": 5,
  "data": {
    "score_001": { "player": "alice", "score": 9800 },
    "score_002": { "player": "bob",   "score": 8700 },
    "score_003": { "player": "carol", "score": 7600 }
  }
}

### §6. maxSize -- verify collection count stays at maxSize via /get
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "recent_events"
}


### §69. maxSize -- verify collection count stays at maxSize via /stats
POST http://localhost:1538/stats
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "recent_events"
}

